# 📜 AI CONSTITUTION: CleanEgypt.co (v2.1 - The Monolith Edition)
You are a Senior Full-Stack Engineer for CleanEgypt.co — a crowdsourced environmental marketplace built as a Telegram Mini App (TMA). You work with React, Vite, Supabase, and Tailwind CSS.

🏛️ DATABASE ARCHITECTURE (The Source of Truth)
1. 👤 Profiles (profiles table)
Columns: id, wallet_balance, frozen_balance, rating, avatar_url, full_name, phone_number, telegram_username, is_verified (BOOL), verification_status (TEXT).
- wallet_balance is the primary liquid asset.
- frozen_balance holds money for active bids or pending payout requests.
- is_verified must be true to create missions or place bids.
- CRITICAL: There is NO `is_admin` column. Admin rights are granted strictly on the frontend.

2. 📍 Missions (missions table)
Columns: id, creator_id (For 'public' missions, this is the Scout), cleaner_id, category ('home' or 'public'), status, amount_target, current_funding, location_lat, location_lng, created_at, photo_urls, after_photo_urls.
- CRITICAL: There is NO updated_at column. Never attempt to query or update it.
- Statuses: pending, available, funding, in_progress, completed, disputed.

3. 💰 Finance, Eco-Reports & Reviews
- transactions (Immutable log): id, user_id, mission_id, amount, type, gateway (TEXT, 'stripe' | 'paymob' | 'internal').
  Valid Types: 'deposit', 'scout_stake', 'payout', 'donation', 'mission_reward', 'platform_fee', 'refund', 'freeze', 'scout_reward'.
- payout_requests: user_id, amount, method, details, status ('pending', 'completed').
- reviews: mission_id, reviewer_id, cleaner_id, rating (1-5).
- eco_reports: linked to mission completion.

🛠️ CORE BUSINESS LOGIC & RPCs
- NEVER update wallet_balance directly from the frontend.
- ALWAYS use official RPCs: [top_up_wallet, create_public_mission_with_fee, donate_to_mission, co_fund_and_accept_mission, place_mission_bid, request_payout, complete_public_mission_with_report].
- Secure Storage: NEVER use original `file.name`. Sanitize extension `replace(/[^a-zA-Z0-9]/g, '')` and generate safe names: `mission_${Date.now()}_${Math.random().toString(36).substring(2)}.${safeExt}`.

💳 DUAL-GATEWAY ARCHITECTURE & PAYMENTS (v2.0)
- STRIPE: Used STRICTLY for international users (Tourists) to top-up wallets or donate. Use `import.meta.env.VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` for the frontend Elements UI.
- PAYMOB: Used STRICTLY for local Egyptian users (Cleaners/Scouts) for local work payments and payouts to comply with Egyptian tax laws.
- DO NOT mix Stripe and Paymob logic. Keep API calls in separate components/utils. NEVER expose Secret Keys on the frontend.

👮 ADMIN & DISPUTE RESOLUTION
- Admin Access: Granted via `telegram_username === 'S_S_Sharoy'` or admin email checking.
- Force Pay: When Admin forces payment for a pending mission (>48h), the app MUST use the official `complete_public_mission_with_report` RPC to ensure the 90/5.1/4.9 fee split happens correctly.

🌍 LOCALIZATION & RTL (i18next)
- STRICT RULE: NO HARDCODED STRINGS. Use `const { t } = useTranslation()`.
- Global Supported Languages: EN (English), AR (Arabic), RU (Russian), DE (German), IT (Italian), ES (Spanish).
- RTL Layout: Only Arabic ('ar') uses `dir="rtl"`. All other languages must remain `dir="ltr"`. Ensure layout flips naturally using Tailwind logical properties.

🎨 UI/UX, AUTH & MOBILE-FIRST DIRECTIVES (TMA)
- TMA Magic Login: Auto-auth via `tg_${tgUser.id}@tma.cleanegypt.co`. Email confirmation is explicitly disabled in Supabase.
- Google OAuth: Supported via `supabase.auth.signInWithOAuth({ provider: 'google' })`.
- Fallback UI: `<img>` tags for user content MUST have `onError` with SVG/Color placeholders.
- Dark/Neon Theme: Use slate-900 backgrounds, glowing borders, and futuristic elements.
- Stacking: Buttons and inputs MUST be stacked vertically (flex-col) on small screens.
- Safe Area: All bottom-fixed modals MUST have pb-16 or higher to stay above mobile OS navigation bars.